{"nodes": [{"id": "github_copilot_instructions", "label": "copilot-instructions.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_schmuckstueck_status_regeln", "label": "Schmuckstueck-Statusregeln (Verfuegbar/Verkauft/Ausschuss/Aktiv Ausgelagert)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verkauft=1 AND Ausschuss=0; Ausschuss=1; Verfuegbar: alle drei 0; Aktiv ausgelagert: Ausgelagert>0 ohne Verkauf/Ausschuss. Verkauft und Ausschuss schliessen sich aus; zentral im WHERE-Builder, damit die Regeln in der ganzen Codebasis konsistent bleiben."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_where_builder_pflicht", "label": "WHERE-Builder-Pflicht fuer Schmuckstueck-Queries", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Alle Schmuckstueck-Filter muessen ueber whereClauseBuilder laufen, damit Statuslogik nicht pro Route auseinanderdriftet. Migriert: dashboard, schmuckstuecke, sumup, kunden, inventur; offen: lieferscheine.js, rechnungen.js. Signatur where(startParamIdx, tenantId) haelt Multi-Mandanten-Faehigkeit offen."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_artikelnummer_praefix_schema", "label": "Artikelnummer-Praefix-Schema (Hersteller/Grundmaterial/Produktart + Suffix)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1. Stelle Hersteller (M=Marina, S=Saskia), 2. Stelle Grundmaterial (A..Y), 3. Stelle Produktart (A/H/O/S); _N-Suffix = Exemplar desselben Typs."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_basis_artikelnummer", "label": "Basis-Artikelnummer als Foto-Schluessel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Foto gilt fuer alle Exemplare (MHO123 -> MHO123_1, MHO123_2), daher kein FK von Foto auf Schmuckstueck."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_in_datenbank", "label": "Fotos als BYTEA in eigener Tabelle (Issue #208/#214)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eigene Tabellen Foto/bestellung_foto, damit SELECT * auf Schmuckstueck keine Bilddaten laedt; Listen liefern nur hatFoto per EXISTS. Alte Spalte Schmuckstueck.Foto per DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS entfernt, kein Datei-Fallback mehr."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_audit_log_hash_chain", "label": "audit_log Hash-Kette und Unveraenderlichkeit (Issue #139)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "trg_audit_log_hash_chain verkettet Zeilen per SHA-256, trg_audit_log_immutable blockiert UPDATE/DELETE; pruefbar per verify_audit_chain() bzw. GET /api/audit-log/verify - Manipulationsschutz des Aenderungsprotokolls."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_e_rechnung_en16931", "label": "E-Rechnung EN 16931 (XRechnung 3.0 CII / ZUGFeRD PDF/A-3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rabatt und Provision als Nachlaesse auf Dokumentebene (BG-20), USt-Kategorie E (Kleinunternehmer Par. 19 UStG). validator.js prueft offline gegen XSD+Schematron, dieselben Artefakte wie der KoSIT-Validator."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_zod_input_validierung", "label": "Zod-Input-Validierung fuer schreibende Routen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ohne Schema gelangen unbekannte Felder und ungepruefte Typen in SQL. Zod strippt unbekannte Felder, wandelt leere Strings zu null und Zahl-Strings zu Zahlen (HTML-Formulare senden alles als String). Tests pruefen bewusst auch den echten Frontend-Payload, damit Schemas nicht zu streng werden."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_cors_allowlist", "label": "CORS-Allowlist ueber ALLOWED_ORIGINS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nur explizit erlaubte Origins; Requests ohne Origin (same-origin, curl, Healthcheck) passieren. In Produktion same-origin, daher meist keine Konfiguration noetig."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_content_security_policy", "label": "Content-Security-Policy via helmet", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CSP an das ausgelieferte Frontend angepasst (img-src data:/blob: fuer Fotos, frame-ancestors none gegen Clickjacking); crossOriginResourcePolicy=cross-origin fuer Vite-Dev-Server."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_tls_reverse_proxy", "label": "TLS-Terminierung im Reverse Proxy (Issue #138)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Express terminiert kein TLS; TRUST_PROXY, FORCE_HTTPS und HSTS_MAX_AGE sind standardmaessig aus, damit native Entwicklung ohne Proxy nicht bricht. Produktion ohne FORCE_HTTPS/COOKIE_SECURE loggt nur eine Warnung statt abzustuerzen."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_double_submit_cookie_csrf", "label": "Double-Submit-Cookie CSRF-Schutz", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bewusst nicht csurf (seit 2022 deprecated). csrfToken-Cookie absichtlich nicht httpOnly, api.js spiegelt ihn in X-CSRF-Token; Vergleich per timingSafeEqual. Greift nur bei Cookie-Auth - Bearer-Clients und oeffentliche Endpunkte sind ausgenommen, da dort keine Ambient Authority existiert."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_httponly_jwt_cookie", "label": "httpOnly-JWT-Cookie statt localStorage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "httpOnly schuetzt vor XSS-Auslesen, sameSite=lax als CSRF-Grundschutz, maxAge 8h passend zur JWT-Laufzeit. Alle Cookie-Attribute zentral in authCookie.js, damit Setzen und Loeschen nicht auseinanderdriften. Bearer-Header bleibt Fallback fuer curl/Playwright."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_account_lockout", "label": "Account-Lockout und Passwort-Reset-Token", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "5 Fehlversuche -> 30 min Sperre; Fehlversuche nur fuer existierende Konten gezaehlt und forgot-password antwortet immer gleich, damit kein Benutzernamen-Orakel entsteht. Nur SHA-256-Hash des Tokens gespeichert. Kein SMTP: Reset-Link geht ins Backend-Log. Rate-Limit allein genuegt nicht, da pro IP."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_legacy_hash_migration", "label": "Stille Migration bcrypt(sha256(pw)) -> bcrypt(pw) (Issue #131)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frontend hashte frueher mit SHA-256 vor. verifyPassword meldet needsRehash; Login stellt beim ersten Erfolg um. Fallback erst entfernen, wenn alle Konten sich einmal angemeldet haben."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_rollenmodell", "label": "Rollenmodell user/bearbeiter/admin", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "user: nur Schmuckstuecke anlegen; bearbeiter: alle Seiten ausser Admin; admin: zusaetzlich Audit-Log, Debug, Benutzerverwaltung, Datensicherung."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_single_image_deployment", "label": "Single-Image-Deployment ohne Nginx", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Multi-Stage-Dockerfile baut Vite-Frontend und kopiert dist/ als public/ ins Express-Image; API und Frontend same-origin auf einem Port."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_json_backup_import", "label": "JSON-Backup mit schema-kompatiblem Import", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Importiert nur Spalten, die in Backup und aktueller DB existieren; Batches a 100 Zeilen wegen PostgreSQL-Parameterlimit; setzt SERIAL-Sequenzen zurueck; transaktional mit Rollback. Foto/bestellung_foto ausgenommen."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_zip_backup", "label": "Foto-ZIP-Sicherung (gestreamt, Upsert-Import als Hintergrund-Job)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Base64 im JSON sprengt bei ~1,6 GB jedes Body-Limit, daher eigenes ZIP ohne Kompression aus REPEATABLE-READ-Snapshot, immer nur ein Foto im Speicher. Import per Upsert und damit wiederholbar; Job-Fortschritt abfragbar. Erledigt das Import-Limit aus #214."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_file_based_secrets", "label": "Secrets per _FILE / getSecret und Produktions-Pruefung", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JWT_SECRET, JWT_SECRET_OLD, DB_PASSWORD, DATABASE_URL, BESTELLUNG_ENCRYPTION_KEY auch als <NAME>_FILE; Start in Produktion bricht bei Platzhalter oder zu kurzem Secret ab."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_keine_inline_styles", "label": "Regel: keine Inline-Styles, nur Klassen in index.css", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zentrale Styles fuer konsistentes Design und einfacheres Refactoring, keine Vermischung von Stil- und Komponentenlogik."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_documentmanager_pattern", "label": "DocumentManager-Pattern (Lieferscheine/Rechnungen)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lieferscheine und Rechnungen teilen ~95% Logik/UI; gemeinsame parametrisierte Komponente, Seiten nur Typ-Konfiguration. Aenderungen zuerst in DocumentManager.jsx."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_mysql_postgres_migration", "label": "MySQL/MariaDB -> PostgreSQL Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Typumstellungen (AUTO_INCREMENT->SERIAL, tinyint->BOOLEAN), Umlaute in Anfuehrungszeichen, ON UPDATE durch Trigger trg_update_letzte_aenderung ersetzt."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_lagerinventur_entwurf", "label": "Lager-Inventur-Entwuerfe (lagerinventur, JSONB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "data = {artikelnummer: anzahl}, status entwurf|abgeschlossen, FK app_users; Soll/Ist-Diff gegen Lagerbestand; per db.js-Startup-Migration angelegt."}, {"id": "github_copilot_instructions_rate_limit_nur_unauthentifiziert", "label": "Rate-Limits nur fuer unauthentifizierte Endpunkte", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Login/Reset max. 20 fehlgeschlagene Versuche/15 min, Bestellformular 10/15 min. Angemeldete App ungedrosselt, weil jede Tabellenzeile einen Foto-Request ausloest. TRUST_PROXY noetig, sonst teilen sich alle Nutzer die Quote einer IP."}], "edges": [{"source": "github_copilot_instructions_where_builder_pflicht", "target": "utils_whereclausebuilder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_schmuckstueck_status_regeln", "target": "utils_whereclausebuilder", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_where_builder_pflicht", "target": "github_copilot_instructions_schmuckstueck_status_regeln", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_basis_artikelnummer", "target": "github_copilot_instructions_artikelnummer_praefix_schema", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_in_datenbank", "target": "utils_fotoservice", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_in_datenbank", "target": "utils_fotoservice_hatfotosql", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_in_datenbank", "target": "config_db_ensurefototables", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_foto_in_datenbank", "target": "github_copilot_instructions_basis_artikelnummer", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_audit_log_hash_chain", "target": "config_db_ensureauditlogtamperprotection", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "github_copilot_instructions_e_rechnung_en16931", "target": "erechnung_validator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".g